        "annotator": 1,
        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nWrite code for a Discord bot using Discord.js v14. The bot has one command, ban. All commands are slash commands.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nvar Discord = require('discord.js');\nvar client = new Discord.Client();\n\n// Define the ban command\nconst ban = '!ban';\n\n// Create a function to handle the ban command\nfunction banHandler(event) {\n    // Get the user who sent the message\n    var user = event.user;\n\n    // Check if the user has been banned before\n    if (user.ban === true) {\n        return;\n    }\n\n    // Check if the user has permission to ban\n    if (!user.permissions.has('BAN')) {\n        return;\n    }\n\n    // If the user does not have any bans, ban them\n    if (user.bans.length === 0) {\n        user.sendMessage(\"You have been banned!\");\n        user.ban = true;\n    }\n\n    // If the user has been banned before, do nothing\n    else {\n        user.sendMessage(\"You have already been banned!\");\n    }\n}\n\n// Listen for the ban command\nclient.on(ban, banHandler);\n\n// Start the bot\nclient.login('TOKEN');\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model's response offer direct, pertinent, and valuable information that actively assists the user's query or concern in a dialogue? The response should align with the user's needs and offer proactive suggestions 