        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nWhat are some Nietzsche's philosophical ideas that still influence modern-day culture?\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nSome of Nietzsche's philosophical ideas that still influence modern-day culture include his idea of the \" vormals stehen \" or \"former standing\", which posits that individuals should attempt to create for themselves a credo or value system largely of their own design. This idea is aimed at helping individuals break away from traditional mores and create a more meaningful and individualized set of values. Additionally, Nietzsche's idea of the \"superman\" has been used to inspire individuals to strive for greatness and become \"over-men\" or \"supermen\" in order to create a better and more just world. His idea of the Ubermensch also speaks to the importance of self-creation, self-determination, and self-overcoming. Nietzsche's ideas regarding the \"death of god\" have also had a profound impact on modern-day culture, inspiring many to seek new spiritual and philosophical ground in the wake of traditional religious systems, as well as to re-evaluate current moral, ethical, and spiritual values. Finally, his idea of the \"will to power\" is also widely embraced as a powerful and empowering notion that endorses the pursuit of power and the acquisition of strength.\n\n##