        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nWrite a short essay on how Adolf Hitler took over germany in 1935.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nAdolf Hitler took over Germany in 1935 through a variety of actions, including the appointment of himself as Chancellor in 1933 and his subsequent establishment of a one-party Nazi state. He also used a combination of propaganda, intimidation and intimidation of opposition, and the suspension of civil liberties to consolidate his power. He also gained huge popularity by exploiting Germany\u2019s economic problems and promising a return to national pride and prosperity. Hitler also pursued an ambitious expansionist foreign policy, leading to the remilitarization of the Rhineland and the Anschluss with Austria in 1938. As the Nazi Party became the only legal political party in Germany, Hitler was able to create a totalitarian state that was ruled by fear and terror. Hitler also used the aggressive and often violent tactics of his paramilitary organization, the SS, to control the population. In addition, Hitler used his powerful oratory and propaganda to manipulate public opinion and build a cult of personality. By 1935, Hitler had secured his hold on Germany and created the totalitarian dictatorship that would lead Germany into World War II.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model's response o