    {
        "source": "helpful_base",
        "annotator": 5,
        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nI like to host guests at my home from time to time, and I am gathering  recipes of different dishes and drinks to keep things interesting. I am interested in trying some Israeli dishes. Can you give me a recipe Israeli Cheese Bourekas?\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nYes, here is a recipe for Israeli Cheese Bourekas:\n\nIngredients:\n- 2 cups of all-purpose flour\n- 2 teaspoons of salt\n- 2 teaspoons of baking powder\n- 1/2 cup of butter\n- 1/2 cup of granulated sugar\n- 1/2 cup of plain yogurt\n- 3/4 cup of grated cheddar cheese \n- 2 eggs\n- 1 tablespoon of freshly ground black pepper  \n- 1/2 cup of warm milk\n- 1/2 cup of chopped fresh parsley\n\nInstructions:\n1. Preheat oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees Celsius). Grease a baking sheet.\n2. In a large bowl, combine the flour, salt, baking powder and butter. Cut in the butter until the mixture resembles coarse crumbs. Stir in the sugar, yogurt, grated cheddar cheese, eggs and pepper.\n3. Knead dough on a lightly floured surface for about 10 seconds. Roll dough into a 1/8 inch thick cylinder. Cut into 12 equal pieces.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model's response offer direct, pertinent, and valuable information that actively assists the user's query or concern in a dialogue? The response should align with the user's needs and offer proactive suggestions or advice, if applicable.]\nScore 1: The model's response is completely off-topic and offers no helpful information or direction in relation to the user's query or concern.\nScore 2: The model's response vaguely addresses the user's query, but it lacks depth, clarity, or relevance, necessitating the user to seek further clarification.\nScore 3: The model's response addresses the user's query, but misses certain key aspects or does not provide additional helpful insights that might be relevant to the user.\nScore 4: The model's response effectively addresses the user's query, providing pertinent information. It might offer some proactive suggestions, but might not cover all potential insights or advice.\nScore 5: The model's response perfectly addresses the user's query, offering direct, comprehensive, and pertinent information. It anticipates further questions and provides proactive suggestions or advice, fully aligning with the user's needs.\n\n###Feedback: ",
        "rejected_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nI like to host guests at my home from time to time, and I am gathering  recipes of different dishes and drinks to keep things interesting. I am interested in trying some Israeli dishes. Can you give me a recipe Israeli Cheese Bourekas?\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nSure! Here is a recipe for Israeli Cheese Bourekas:\r\n\r\nIngredients: \r\n- 2 packages of puff pastry\r\n- 2 cups of grated cheese (feta or mozzarella)\r\n- 2 tablespoons of chopped parsley \r\n- 1 tablespoon of sesame seeds\r\n- 2 beaten eggs\r\n- 2 tablespoons of melted butter \r\n\r\nInstructions: \r\n1. Preheat oven to 375\u00b0F.\r\n2. Place puff pastry on a lightly floured surface and roll out to 1/8 inch thickness. Cut into 3-inch circles. \r\n3. Place a tablespoon of grated cheese, 1/2 teaspoon of parsley, and 1/4 teaspoon of sesame seeds in the center of each circle. \r\n4. Paint the edges of the circles with beaten egg and fold the edges together to form a half moon shape. \r\n5. Place bourekas on a greased baking sheet. \r\n6. Brush the tops of the bourekas with melted butter and sprinkle with sesame seeds. \r\n7. Bake for 15-20 minutes until golden brown. \r\n8. Serve warm. Enjoy!\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model's response offer direct, pertinent, and valuable information that actively assists the user's query or concern in a dialogue? The response should align with the user's needs and offer proactive suggestions or advice, if applicable.]\nScore 1: The model's response is completely off-topic and offers no helpful information or direction in relation to the user's query or concern.\nScore 2: The model's response vaguely addresses the user's query, but it lacks depth, clarity, or relevance, necessitating the user to seek further clarification.\nScore 3: The model's response addresses the user's query, but misses certain key aspects or does not provide additional helpful insights that might be relevant to the user.\nScore 4: The model's response effectively addresses the user's query, providing pertinent information. It might offer some proactive suggestions, but might not cover all potential insights or advice.\nScore 5: The model's response perfectly addresses the user's query, offering direct, comprehensive, and pertinent information. It anticipates further questions and provides proactive suggestions or advice, fully aligning with the user's needs.\n\n###Feedback: "
