        "rejected_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nI like to host guests at my home from time to time, and I am gathering  recipes of different dishes and drinks to keep things interesting. I am interested in trying some Israeli dishes. Can you give me a recipe Israeli Cheese Bourekas?\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nIsraeli Cheese Bourekas:\n- 2 tablespoons all-purpose flour\n- 2 tablespoons semolina flour\n- 1 teaspoon baking powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon salt\n- 2 tablespoons butter\n- 2 tablespoons of minced onion\n- 2 tablespoons of minced garlic\n- 5 ounces of cheese\n- 3 eggs\n- 2 tablespoons of fresh parsley, minced\n- 2 tablespoons of fresh dill, minced\n\nIn a medium bowl, combine the flour, semolina flour, baking powder, and salt. Cut in the butter and mix until the mixture resembles coarse crumbs. Stir in the onion and garlic and mix until evenly distributed. Add the cheese and eggs and mix until evenly distributed. Add the parsley and dill and mix until evenly distributed. \n\nPour the mixture into a greased 9x13-inch baking dish. Bake in the preheated oven for 45 minutes, or until a knife inserted in the center of the bourekas comes out clean. Allow to cool before serving.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model's response offer direct, pertinent, and valuable information that actively assists the user's query or concern in a dia