        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nCompose an engaging travel blog post about a recent trip to Hawaii, highlighting cultural experiences and must-see attractions.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nMy recent trip to Hawaii was one of the most amazing experiences I have had. From the stunning beaches and lush foliage to the warm and welcoming people, there is something for everyone in Hawaii. \r\n\r\nI was amazed by the culture of the islands. From the traditional hula performances and luaus to the unique and vibrant art scene, there is no shortage of cultural experiences to immerse yourself in. I particularly enjoyed learning about the history of the Hawaiian islands and the stories of the indigenous people. \r\n\r\nIn terms of attractions, there are plenty of must-see places. I highly recommend taking a boat tour of the Na Pali coast, snorkeling in the crystal clear waters of Hanauma Bay, and exploring the majestic volcanic landscape of the Hawaii Volcanoes National Park. \r\n\r\nAll in all, my trip to Hawaii was an unforgettable experience. From the breathtaking scenery and cultural experiences to the incredibly friendly locals, it's a destination I highly recommend to anyone looking for a unique and unforgettable adventure.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model's response offer direct, pertinent, and valuable information that actively assists the user's query or concern in a dialogue? The response should align with the user's needs and offer proactive suggestions or advice, if applicable.]\nScore 1: The model's response is completely off-topic and offers no helpful information or direction in relation to the user's query or concern.\nScore 2: The model's response vaguely addresses the user's query, but it lacks depth, clarity, or relevance, necessitating the user to seek further clarification.\nScore 3: The model's response addresses the user's query, but misses certain key aspects or does not provide additional helpful insights that might be relevant to the user.\nScore 4: The model's response effectively addresses the user's query, providing pertinent information. It might offer some proactive suggestions, but might not cover all potential insights or advice.\nScore 5: The model's response perfectly addresses the user's query, offering direct, comprehensive, and pertinent information. It anticipates further questions and provides proactive suggestions or advice, fully aligning with the user's needs.\n\n###Feedback: ",
        "rejected_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nCompose an engaging travel blog post about a recent trip to Hawaii, highlighting cultural experiences and must-see attractions.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nAfter months of anticipation, I finally had the chance to embark on a trip to the tropical paradise of Hawaii! From sprawling beaches to lush jungles, this unique part of the world offers visitors a myriad of amazing experiences. \n\nI had the chance to visit two of the main islands, Oahu and Maui. On Oahu, I had the chance to explore the bustling city of Honolulu and take in the stunning views of the north shore. I also visited the majestic Kamehameha Iwa statue at Pu\u2019oloa, ran along the breathtaking Halona Beach Cove, and ate my first authentic plate of Spam musubi. \n\nOn Maui, I was fortunate enough to take part in several cultural activities. I sampled the succulent ohi\u2019a lehua fruit, visited an ancient ahupua\u2019a land division, learned the history of sugar production in Hawaii, and watched a traditional hula performance. I also had the chance to explore the iconic Road to Hana, take a sunrise hike, and snorkel the coral reefs of Molokini.\n\nOverall, my trip to Hawaii was truly unforgettable and I am so grateful for the amazing cultural experiences and breathtaking natural sights that it afforded me. I\n\n###